  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the person experiencing discomfort",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the person making a face of discomfort with hands framing their eyes, as this visual serves as a proxy for the user's own experience of chopping onions. The meme implicitly invites the viewer to identify with the person's reaction, creating a shared, relatable experience. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you', but the universal nature of the experience and the exaggerated expression create an implicit 'you' projection.",
